    "instruction": "Create a skip link that is visually hidden until it receives focus, then jumps keyboard users straight to the main content.",
    "output": "<style>\n  .skip-link {\n    position: absolute; left: -9999px; top: 0;\n    background: #0f172a; color: #fff; padding: .75rem 1.25rem;\n    text-decoration: none; border-radius: 0 0 8px 0; z-index: 100;\n  }\n  .skip-link:focus { left: 0; outline: 3px solid #f59e0b; outline-offset: 2px; }\n  #main:focus { outline: none; }\n</style>\n<a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to main content</a>\n<header>\n  <nav aria-label=\"Primary\"><a href=\"#\">Home</a> <a href=\"#\">Docs</a></nav>\n</header>\n<main id=\"main\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n  <h1>Page content starts here</h1>\n  <p>Keyboard users tabbing from the top land directly in this region.</p>\n</main>"
