    "instruction": "Replace failing low-contrast text colors with WCAG AA compliant colors and show the before and after swatches.",
    "output": "<style>\n  .before { color: #b0b0b0; background: #fff; }  /* fails AA: about 2.1:1 */\n  .after  { color: #595959; background: #fff; }  /* passes AA: about 7:1 */\n  .muted-aa { color: #6b7280; background: #f9fafb; } /* passes: 4.83:1 */\n  .chip { display: inline-block; padding: .5rem .9rem; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; margin: 0 .75rem .75rem 0; }\n</style>\n<div>\n  <span class=\"chip before\">Fails contrast</span>\n  <span class=\"chip after\">Passes AA</span>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted-aa\">Body text at #6b7280 on #f9fafb clears the 4.5:1 requirement.</p>"
